# Kaskad SSH menu texts: area guide — item 13 “Guide” (show_instructions). Key prefix GUIDE_. English.
# Format as in core.en.sh. A page: GUIDE_P<n>_T — title, GUIDE_P<n> — text (printf format: \n — new line, %s — colour
# and the kaskadctl path from the code, in the same order as in guide.ru.sh). Up to 16 lines with the title, 78 columns.
M_en_GUIDE_NEXT='Next'
M_en_GUIDE_PREV='Back'
M_en_GUIDE_GOTO='Go to page'
M_en_GUIDE_EXIT='Quit'
M_en_GUIDE_BAD='No such item: a page number from 1 to %s, N — next, P — back, 0 — quit.'
M_en_GUIDE_P1_T='WHAT IS A CASCADE'
M_en_GUIDE_P1='A bridge: Client → This server → VPN abroad → Internet\nYour ISP sees only a Russian IP.\n\nYou need: a VPS in Russia + a VPN abroad + its IP:Port\n\n%sPhones and routers through this server — item 17.%s The wizard installs\nprotocols, adds a device and shows which app to install and what to tap\non the phone (pp. 9–11).\nItems 1–4 — port forwards to your VPN abroad (pp. 2–3).\nItem 16 — forwarding engine and migration: settings backup to another\nserver (p. 8).\nItem 20 — Quick Start in the browser. Server check — 21 and p. 12'
M_en_GUIDE_P2_T='AWG/VLESS/MTProto'
M_en_GUIDE_P2='1) AWG: UDP, port 51820\n2) VLESS: TCP, port 443\n3) MTProto: TCP, port 8443\n\nAfter you enter the IP — automatic GeoIP + ping test\n\nOn the nftables engine (menu 16):\n  • a forward works only for this server’s addresses: it does not\n    intercept transit traffic (Docker, gateway clients);\n  • port in use (SSH, a server service, Docker) — Kaskad says so and\n    asks whether to add it anyway.'
M_en_GUIDE_P3_T='CUSTOM / FORWARDS'
M_en_GUIDE_P3='4) Custom: different ports, SSH/RDP\n5) Forwards: table with cascade IPs + GeoIP + traffic of each forward\n   (traffic — on the nftables engine)\n14) Server names + notes\n\nOn nftables, forwarding the SSH port cuts off SSH to the server itself:\nKaskad asks you to type the word CONFIRM. Other ports in use — the\nquestion “Add anyway?” and a numbered choice. The bot refuses in such\ncases: you can confirm only in the menu.'
M_en_GUIDE_P4_T='PING'
M_en_GUIDE_P4='6) Live Ping with an ASCII chart:\n  ▓▓▓░░░░░ — green (<50 ms)\n  ▓▓▓▓▓▓░░ — yellow (50–100 ms)\n  ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ — red (>100 ms)\n  ████████ — TIMEOUT'
M_en_GUIDE_P5_T='MONITORING'
M_en_GUIDE_P5='7) Auto checks with alerts in Telegram\nIntervals: 10s / 1min / 5min\nAlerts: 10s / 60s / 5min / 15min\nThe service starts and stops on its own'
M_en_GUIDE_P6_T='TELEGRAM BOT'
M_en_GUIDE_P6='8) @BotFather → token → Chat ID → start\nTwo menu modes:\n  Inline — buttons under the message\n  Reply — large buttons at the bottom of the screen\nSwitch: a button in the menu or /inline'
M_en_GUIDE_P7_T='BOT FEATURES'
M_en_GUIDE_P7='Forwards, Ping (1x/10x/60s), Monitoring\n💻 System: CPU/RAM/Swap/Disk/processes\n🏢 Hosting: promo codes\nGeoIP + ping test when adding\nServer names + notes\nOn nftables the bot refuses if the port is in use: add the forward in the menu'
M_en_GUIDE_P8_T='ENGINE AND MIGRATION (16)'
M_en_GUIDE_P8='Forwards live in the nftables table “kaskad” (in 2.x — iptables rules).\nA forward works only for this server’s addresses; each shows its traffic\n(menu 5 “Forwards”). The kaskad-net and kaskad-net-watch services load the\ntable at boot and repair it every minute if someone flushed the rules.\n\nMigration from old Kaskad (free or PRO 2.x): on the first start 3.x shows\nwhat it will move and asks — 1 Migrate now, 2 Later, 3 Don’t ask again.\nA backup first, then a check; if it fails, everything is rolled back by\nitself. Ufw, Docker and other programs’ rules are left alone.\n\n%s16 → 1%s  Switch to nftables           %s16 → 3%s  Backups\n%s16 → 2%s  Bring back iptables (2.13 format, the program stays 3.x)\n%s16 → 4%s  Go back to Kaskad 2.13 (the gateway is removed)\n%s16 → 6%s  Settings backup file: move to another server, undo'
M_en_GUIDE_P9_T='GATEWAY (17): WHAT IT IS'
M_en_GUIDE_P9='A phone, computer or router connects to this server with an app\n(AmneziaVPN, WireGuard) or a built-in VPN (L2TP/IPsec, IKEv2) and goes\nonline through your VPN abroad (an “exit”) or from the server’s address.\n\n  device → this server → your VPN abroad → internet\n\nThe first time, 17 opens the wizard: check → protocols → ports → exit (a\nvless:// or vpn:// key of your VPN) → install → first device. Right after\nthat — device settings: what to install, what to copy, what to tap.\nNeeds Debian 12/13 or Ubuntu 24.04/26.04+. Forwards (1–5) are not touched.\nDevices can’t see each other; the server’s private networks are closed.\n%s17 → 4%s client address · %s17 → 6%s turn off · %s17 → 7%s remove gateway'
M_en_GUIDE_P10_T='PROTOCOLS AND DEVICES'
M_en_GUIDE_P10='%s17 → 1%s Protocols — installed as you choose:\n  WireGuard, AmneziaWG (lines 1.5, 2.0, 3.1), L2TP/IPsec — checked in wizard\n  IKEv2, SSTP, OpenVPN, OpenConnect, SOCKS5, VLESS Reality — optional\n  PPTP — only for old routers: weak encryption\n  In a protocol card: turn on/off, change the port, remove;\n  for VLESS also the masking site and new server keys.\n\n%s17 → 2%s Users & devices: user → devices → protocols.\n  “Issue settings” — for the device’s OS: QR, vpn:// link, .conf or\n  .ovpn file, .mobileconfig profile, PowerShell script, fields to type in.\n  “Change keys and passwords” — settings issued earlier stop working.\n  Changed the address (17 → 4) or a protocol port — reissue the settings.\n  Keys and passwords are shown only on the issue screen (and in files in\n  /root/kaskad-issue — if you ask): don’t send them in the open.'
M_en_GUIDE_P11_T='EXITS AND ROUTES'
M_en_GUIDE_P11='Exits are keys of your VPN abroad (VLESS, AmneziaWG, Hysteria2 and more) from\nthe “Telegram API proxy” pool (the bot’s too: %s8 → 7%s). Add a key: %s17 → 3 → %s%s.\nExit status: “working” / “down: reason” / “not checked yet”.\n\nRoute: of the device (%s17 → 2 → 6%s), else of the user (%s17 → 2 → 7%s),\nelse the default one (%s17 → 3%s):\n  pool      a live exit of the pool; if it dies, the device moves on\n  exit      only the chosen exit\n  direct    from this server’s address\n  block     no internet\nNo live exit — no internet, not “direct” (“on failure — block” by\ndefault). Direct only by explicit choice: the route “direct” or\n“on failure — direct” (%s17 → 3 → 2%s, with the route through the exits).'
M_en_GUIDE_P12_T='IF SOMETHING IS WRONG'
M_en_GUIDE_P12='Action log        %stail -n 50 /var/log/kaskad.log%s\nGateway status    menu %s17 → 5%s or %s%s gw status%s\nEngine status     menu %s16%s (at the top) or %s%s net status%s\nGateway services  %sjournalctl -u '\''kaskad-gw-*'\'' -n 50%s\n\nA forward doesn’t work — item 5: are the port and target right? Menu 16:\nis the table in place?\nA device can’t connect — 17 → 1: is the protocol “working”? Is the port\nopen at the hosting provider? Is the client address (17 → 4) right?\nConnected but no internet — 17 → 3: is the exit “working”? Which route?\n\nBring back iptables: %s16 → 2%s.  Back to Kaskad 2.13: %s16 → 4%s (gateway removed).\nBackups: /var/backups/kaskad (%s16 → 3%s).'
